   Under the BGP configuration, reference the route resolution filter to enforce the tunnel selection.

   ```bash
   configure router bgp
       group "EBGP_PEERS"
           family ipv4
           peer-as <AS_NUMBER>
           neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
               import "BGP_IN_POLICY"
               export "BGP_OUT_POLICY"
               resolution-filter "ALLOWED_TUNNELS"  # Apply the filter here
           exit
       exit
       no shutdown
       commit
   ```

3. **(Optional) Global Route Resolution Settings**  
   If you want to apply this restriction globally (not just per-neighbor), modify the `resolution` settings in the base BGP config:

   ```bash
   configure router bgp
       resolution
           filter "ALLOWED_TUNNELS"  # Enforce globally
       exit
       commit
   ```

