        family ipv4
            tunnel-next-hop rsvp ldp
```
Or apply it globally under BGP group or policy:
```bash
configure router policy-options
    policy-statement "TUNNEL_NH"
        entry 10
            action accept
            tunnel-next-hop rsvp ldp
    commit
```

Apply this policy to incoming/outgoing routes:
```bash
configure router bgp
    neighbor <IP>
        import "TUNNEL_NH"
        export "TUNNEL_NH"
```

#### **2. Ensure Route Resolution via Tunnels**
Verify that the BGP next-hop is resolvable via the tunnel:
```bash
show router route-table <BGP_next_hop>
show router tunnel-table <BGP_next_hop>
```
If the tunnel isn’t being used, check IGP (OSPF/IS-IS) metrics—tunnels might lose to direct paths.

