# Configuring BGP Next-Hop Resolution with Lower-Priority OSPF Instances on Nokia 7750 SR

To make BGP prefer next-hop resolution via lower-priority OSPF instances (rather than the highest-priority one) for SR tunnel selection, you'll need to adjust the route table preferences and possibly use routing policies.

## Solution Options:

### Option 1: Adjust Route Table Preferences
```
configure {
    router "Base" {
        bgp {
            next-hop-resolution {
                shortcut-tunnels {
                    family ipv4 {
                        resolution-filter {
                            ospf true
                        }
                        resolution preference 10   # Higher number = lower preference
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Option 2: Use Routing Policies to Influence Selection
Create a policy that modifies the preference for specific routes:
```
configure {
    policy-options {
        policy-statement "prefer-lower-ospf" {
            entry 10 {
                from {
                    protocol ospf
                    instance <lower-priority-instance-id>
                }
                action {
                    preference <higher-value>  # Lower preference value wins
                    accept
                }
            }
        }
    }
    router "Base" {
        bgp {
            import "prefer-lower-ospf"
        }
    }
}
```

### Option 3: Explicit Tunnel Binding (More Direct Control)
If you know the specific tunnel endpoints:
```
configure {
    router "Base" {
        bgp {
            next-hop-resolution {
                labeled-routes {
                    family ipv4 {
                        static-tunnel-routes {
                            prefix <next-hop-ip/32> {
                                resolution-filter {
                                    sr-isis true   # Or SR-OSPF if applicable
                                }
                                preference 20      # Make this higher than default
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Key points:
- Higher preference numbers mean lower actual preference in Nokia's implementation
- You may need to combine approaches depending on your exact topology
- Verify with `show router bgp next-hop-resolution` after changes

